examples.question_text:
$6$ distinct points are marked on a circle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) circle (1.6);
\foreach \angle/\label in {90/A,30/B,-30/C,-90/D,-150/E,150/F}{
\fill (\angle:1.6) circle (1.5pt);
\path (\angle:1.95) node {$\label$};
}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(a) How many straight lines can be drawn through pairs of points?
(b) How many triangles can be formed using these points as vertices?
